===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|side-slip}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|side|slip}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|aviation}} A [[flight]] [[manoeuvre]] that uses [[opposing]] [[rudder]] and [[aileron]] [[input]]s to move the [[aircraft]] [[sideways]] without [[turn]]ing it.
## {{lb|en|aviation}} A flight [[maneuver]] to [[rapidly]] [[lose]] [[speed]] and/or [[altitude]] whilst not [[alter]]ing the aircraft's ground [[track]].
# {{lb|en|aviation}} A flight condition where an aircraft's [[longitudinal]] [[axis]] is not aligned with its [[direction]] of [[motion]] [[relative]] to the [[surround]]ing [[air]].
# {{lb|en|aviation|uncountable|by extension}} The [[angle]] between an aircraft's longitudinal axis and its direction of motion relative to the surrounding air.

